  "interpretation": {
    "map_public": "The synthetic data module places filler at _DATA+0 and _global_word at _DATA+2. RTLink map shows _global_word at linear 0000:0006 and DGROUP first-layout-origin 0000:0004; MS LINK map shows DGROUP frame paragraph base 0000:0000, _DATA at 00004h, and _global_word at 0006h.",
    "observed": "Both linkers put 0006h in the LOC1 field, with no MZ relocation. F5 target-derived frame uses the paragraph frame base (DS value * 16), not the first initialized byte shown as RTLink group layout origin; in this fixture frame base is zero, so symbol linear offset 6 is the expected encoded value. This is consistent with MSC6 F5/T6 semantics.",
    "raw_omf": "LOC1 at _TEXT+1 has raw field 0000, frame method 5 (target-derived), target method 6 external _global_word, no encoded displacement; target/frame thread declarations are preserved in preceding FIXUPP record."
  },
